{# How to see what a collection holds and how to find a file by its name. Each sentence that
   names a tool renders only when the run has it. #}
Folders and files

{% if has('list_collections') %}
{{ tool('list_collections') }} gives the collections of this chat and the datasets in each.

{% endif %}
{% if has('folder_overview') %}
1. {{ tool('folder_overview') }} gives the storage counts of each collection and dataset.
{% endif %}
{% if has('folder_list') %}
2. {{ tool('folder_list') }} gives the child folders and the files of one folder of a dataset. Go down one folder at a time.
{% endif %}
{% if has('folder_search') %}
3. To find a folder or a file by its name inside one dataset, call {{ tool('folder_search') }}.
{% endif %}
{% if has('search_collections') %}
4. To find a file by its name in every collection, call {{ tool('search_collections') }} with filename_only set to true. Give the name or a part of it as the query.
{% endif %}
{% if has('search_histogram') %}
5. {{ tool('search_histogram') }} counts the documents of a search by date or by size. Use it to see which years a collection covers before you set a date filter.
{% endif %}
{% if has('search_facet_values') %}
6. {{ tool('search_facet_values') }} gives the values of a filter, for example the file types, with their counts.
{% endif %}

A file name or a path is not a document id. To read a file that you found by its name, copy the file_hash of its result row.
